    "explanation": "Within the comparable base ST1-ST5, ST5 accounts for 2,607,588.7038 of revenue Growth, or 74.2338% of the total change, taking revenue to 3,214,635.1092 from 607,046.4054; the scan also shows this move is overwhelmingly associated with higher volume, with 1,705,150.8499 of QTY Growth and 640,871 bills growth. A complete ST5-by-item_category_name probe shows the gain was broad but highly concentrated in a few categories, led by PROVISIONS at 867,279.1959 revenue Growth, REFRIDGERATED GOODS at 330,959.1285, GREEN GROCERIES at 286,236.9279, PERSONAL CARE at 220,522.2516, and SPICE MARKET at 164,524.176, all alongside substantial quantity and bill increases. That pattern suggests ST5's outsized growth is likely associated more with expanded selling activity and basket flow across core everyday categories than with a pure rate change, which is consistent with the earlier price-volume split showing about 97% of the revenue uplift tied to volume. Best follow-up check: drill ST5 further from item_category_name into product_group_name within the largest category, especially PROVISIONS, to identify which specific groups carry most of the 867,279.1959 increase.",
