    "explanation": "ST4 accounts for 1,186,833.168 of revenue Growth, or 33.7872% of the comparable ST1-ST5 total change, and the reused decomposition shows 1,086,798.3777 of that increase, 91.5713%, sat in the revenue-per-unit rate rather than quantity. A complete ST4 merchandise cut by 'MIS_DEEP_DIVE2'[item_category_name] shows the uplift was concentrated in a few larger areas: MENS APPAREL added 217,209.2436 on 47,572 extra units, PERSONAL CARE added 188,853.0795 on 58,309 units, LADIES APPAREL added 185,630.3541 on 61,079 units, ENTERTAINMENTS added 175,617.8118 on 15,239 units, and PROVISIONS added 130,864.6125 despite QTY Growth of -141,067.30419. That pattern is associated with a mix/rate-led improvement concentrated in apparel, personal care, entertainment, and provisions rather than a broad storewide unit surge; PROVISIONS is the clearest example where revenue rose while units fell. Best next follow-up check: drill ST4 within the model from these leading item categories into 'MIS_DEEP_DIVE2'[product_group_name] to identify which sub-groups inside PROVISIONS and the apparel categories carried the rate-led gain.",
